-          "quote": "This algorithm performs one finite-budget LM trial update. Inputs are $x\\in U$, a residual function $r:U\\to\\mathbb R^m$, its Jacobian $J(x)$, a fixed nonsingular $D\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$, a floor $\\lambda_{\\min}>0$, current damping $\\lambda\\ge\\lambda_{\\min}$, factors $\\gamma>1$, $0<\\eta_1<\\eta_2<1$, a trust radius $\\Delta>0$, and an attempt cap $N\\ge1$. A computed run may include a certificate that the exact scalar product $J(x)^Tr(x)$ is zero. Put $\\phi(x)=\\|r(x)\\|_2^2/2$ and $m_0(p)=\\|r(x)+J(x)p\\|_2^2/2$. The returned step is obtained by minimizing\n$$\\tfrac12\\|r(x)+J(x)p\\|_2^2+\\tfrac\\lambda2\\|Dp\\|_2^2,$$\nwhich is equivalent to solving\n$$(J(x)^TJ(x)+\\lambda D^TD)p=-J(x)^Tr(x).$$\nFor stable linear algebra, form $A_\\lambda=[J(x);\\sqrt\\lambda D]$ and $s_\\lambda=[r(x);0]$, then call [[alg-gauss-newton-qr-svd-step-with-rank-safeguard]] in QR mode on $(A_\\lambda,s_\\lambda)$. The exact augmented matrix has full column rank because $D$ is nonsingular and $\\lambda>0$. A computed-candidate status remains a candidate and carries no convergence guarantee.\n\nFor attempts $j=1,\\ldots,N$, do the following.\n\n1. If the linear solver reports a factorization, rank, or solve failure, return linear-solve-failure with its report. In exact arithmetic, if $J(x)^Tr(x)=0$, return stationary without forming a ratio. In a computed run, return stationary only with the supplied certificate that this exact gradient is zero; a rounded zero without such a certificate returns gradient-unverified and no ratio.\n2. For a nonzero trial $p$, compute $\\operatorname{pred}=m_0(0)-m_0(p)$. If $\\operatorname{pred}\\le0$, return nonpositive-predicted-decrease; do not compute a ratio.\n3. If $x+p\\notin U$ or $\\|Dp\\|_2>\\Delta$, reject the trial, set $\\lambda\\leftarrow\\gamma\\lambda$, and continue. If the damping update is not representable in the selected arithmetic, return damping-range-failure.\n4. Otherwise compute $\\operatorname{ared}=\\phi(x)-\\phi(x+p)$ and $\\rho=\\operatorname{ared}/\\operatorname{pred}$. If $\\rho<\\eta_1$, reject and set $\\lambda\\leftarrow\\gamma\\lambda$. If this was attempt $N$, return rejection-budget-exhausted; otherwise continue.\n5. If $\\rho\\ge\\eta_1$, accept and return $x+p$, $p$, $\\rho$, and the next damping. If also $\\rho\\ge\\eta_2$ and $\\|Dp\\|_2=\\Delta$, set $\\lambda_{\\rm next}=\\max\\{\\lambda_{\\min},\\lambda/\\gamma\\}$; in every other accepted case set $\\lambda_{\\rm next}=\\lambda$. A failed function evaluation returns trial-evaluation-failure.\n\nIf all $N$ attempts are rejected, return rejection-budget-exhausted. The equality in the boundary test is exact for exact arithmetic and is the equality test on stored values in a computed run. No claim is made that every finite budget succeeds.",
+          "quote": "This algorithm performs one finite-budget LM trial update. Inputs are $x\\in U$, a residual function $r:U\\to\\mathbb R^m$, its Jacobian $J(x)$, a fixed nonsingular $D\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$, an arithmetic mode (exact or computed), a floor $\\lambda_{\\min}>0$, current damping $\\lambda\\ge\\lambda_{\\min}$, factors $\\gamma>1$, $0<\\eta_1<\\eta_2<1$, a trust radius $\\Delta>0$, and an attempt cap $N\\ge1$. A computed run may include a certificate that the exact scalar product $J(x)^Tr(x)$ is zero. Put $\\phi(x)=\\|r(x)\\|_2^2/2$ and $m_0(p)=\\|r(x)+J(x)p\\|_2^2/2$. In exact mode the step is the unique minimizer of\n$$\\tfrac12\\|r(x)+J(x)p\\|_2^2+\\tfrac\\lambda2\\|Dp\\|_2^2,$$\nwhich is equivalent to solving\n$$(J(x)^TJ(x)+\\lambda D^TD)p=-J(x)^Tr(x).$$\nIn computed mode the returned vector is only a candidate for this same subproblem; no exact minimizer claim is made.\n\n\nFor attempts $j=1,\\ldots,N$, do the following with the current damping. After a damping change, construct a new augmented matrix and obtain a report for that actual matrix; do not reuse an earlier damping value's factorization or report.\n\n1. In exact arithmetic, if $J(x)^Tr(x)=0$, return stationary before calling the linear solver. In a computed run, return stationary before the solve only with the supplied certificate that this exact gradient is zero; if computing $J(x)^Tr(x)$ fails, return gradient-evaluation-failure; if the computed product is a rounded zero without that certificate, return gradient-unverified and do not form a ratio. Otherwise perform the augmented construction and linear solve afresh inside this attempt at its current damping: Form $A_\\lambda=[J(x);\\sqrt\\lambda D]$ and $s_\\lambda=[r(x);0]$, then call [[alg-gauss-newton-qr-svd-step-with-rank-safeguard]] in QR mode on $(A_\\lambda,s_\\lambda)$. Exact mode uses the exact positive square root and requires a supplied exact reduced factorization of $A_\\lambda$ for each call; absence of that factorization returns linear-solve-failure. This matrix has full column rank because $D$ is nonsingular and $\\lambda>0$. In computed mode, copy the stored $J(x)$ and $r(x)$ into the top blocks, compute $t=\\operatorname{fl}(\\sqrt\\lambda)$, then fill the bottom block entries $\\operatorname{fl}(tD_{ij})$ in increasing row and column order and fill the appended residual entries with exact zeros. Any first arithmetic or range failure in this construction returns linear-solve-failure with its stage and indices. The call receives a computed QR report for this actual stored $A_\\lambda$. A computed-candidate is usable only when that report includes the low-level procedure's independently verified full-rank certificate $s_\\lambda>0$ for the actual stored matrix, namely $\\|A_\\lambda v\\|_2\\ge s_\\lambda\\|v\\|_2$ for every $v\\in\\mathbb R^n$. Pass this bound as the computed report's certificate field; it is not inferred from a nonzero computed diagonal or from positive definiteness of the ideal exact system alone. A rank-unverified report and every other status besides exact-step in exact mode or computed-candidate in computed mode are unusable and return linear-solve-failure with the report. A computed-candidate remains a candidate and carries no convergence guarantee. If the solver status is not exact-step in exact mode or computed-candidate in computed mode, return linear-solve-failure with its report; in particular, rank-unverified is a failure, not a usable trial.\n2. If exact mode returns $p=0$ after the nonzero-gradient check, return linear-solve-failure with the inconsistent exact solve report. If computed mode returns $p=0$, return zero-step-unverified and do not compute a ratio. For every remaining candidate $p$ (the zero candidates have already returned a status), compute $\\operatorname{pred}=m_0(0)-m_0(p)$. If this computation fails, return model-evaluation-failure; if $\\operatorname{pred}\\le0$, return nonpositive-predicted-decrease. In either case do not compute a ratio.\n3. If computing $x+p$ or $Dp$ fails in the selected arithmetic, return trial-evaluation-failure. If $x+p\\notin U$ or $\\|Dp\\|_2>\\Delta$, reject the trial and compute the damping update $\\lambda^+=\\gamma\\lambda$ in the selected arithmetic. If that update fails, is nonfinite, or is outside the representable range, return damping-range-failure with the current $x,\\lambda$ and the trial report. Otherwise set $\\lambda\\leftarrow\\lambda^+$ and continue.\n4. Otherwise evaluate $r(x+p)$ and compute $\\operatorname{ared}=\\phi(x)-\\phi(x+p)$ and $\\rho=\\operatorname{ared}/\\operatorname{pred}$. A failed trial evaluation or nonfinite computed result returns trial-evaluation-failure. If $\\rho<\\eta_1$, reject and compute $\\lambda^+=\\gamma\\lambda$ in the selected arithmetic. If that damping update fails, is nonfinite, or is outside the representable range, return damping-range-failure with the current $x,\\lambda$ and the trial report. Otherwise set $\\lambda\\leftarrow\\lambda^+$. If this was attempt $N$, return rejection-budget-exhausted; otherwise continue.\n5. If $\\rho\\ge\\eta_1$, first determine the next damping. If also $\\rho\\ge\\eta_2$ and $\\|Dp\\|_2=\\Delta$, compute $q=\\lambda/\\gamma$ in exact mode and $q=\\operatorname{fl}(\\lambda/\\gamma)$ in computed mode. If this division fails, has a nonfinite or nonpositive result, or is outside the representable range, return damping-range-failure with the current $x,\\lambda$ and the trial report, without accepting that trial. Otherwise set $\\lambda_{\\rm next}=\\max\\{\\lambda_{\\min},q\\}$. In every other accepted case set $\\lambda_{\\rm next}=\\lambda$. Only after the next damping is available, accept and return $x+p$, $p$, $\\rho$, and $\\lambda_{\\rm next}$.\n\nIf all $N$ attempts are rejected, return rejection-budget-exhausted. The equality in the boundary test is exact for exact arithmetic and is the equality test on stored values in a computed run. No claim is made that every finite budget succeeds.",
