-          "quote": "Input a stored residual $r\\in\\mathbb R^m$, a stored Jacobian $J\\in\\mathbb R^{m\\times n}$ with $m,n\\ge1$ (using the convention of [[def-jacobian-matrix-and-gradient]]), a factorization mode QR or SVD, and a declared singular-value threshold $\\tau\\ge0$. A computed QR report may also carry a verified full-rank certificate $s>0$ asserting $\\|Jv\\|_2\\ge s\\|v\\|_2$ for every $v\\in\\mathbb R^n$. The target exact step, when it is returned, is the unique minimizer of $\\frac12\\|r+Jp\\|_2^2$ and hence solves $J^TJp=-J^Tr$; this target is asserted only on a full-column-rank branch. Do not form $J^TJ$ in either solve path.\n\nFor QR mode, either supply an exact reduced factorization $J=QR$ with $Q^TQ=I_n$, or compute one by setting $C=[J\\mid-r]$ and, for $k=1,\\ldots,n$, applying [[alg-scaled-householder-reflector-formation-and-application]] to the active part of column $k$ and all trailing columns of $C$, including its last right-hand-side column. Propagate the first factorization failure. In exact mode, a zero diagonal in $R$ returns rank-deficient; otherwise solve $Rp=Q^T(-r)$ by backward substitution and return exact-step($p$). In computed mode, a zero diagonal returns rank-deficient-candidate; a failed triangular solve returns linear-solve-failure; and a nonzero computed diagonal without an independently supplied full-rank certificate returns rank-unverified with the computed candidate but no full-rank claim. With a full-rank certificate, return computed-candidate($p$). The computed-QR backward-stability conclusion of [[thm-computed-full-rank-least-squares-backward-stability]] is attached only when all of that theorem's successful-execution, arithmetic, and nonsingularity hypotheses are supplied; otherwise no backward-stability conclusion is returned.\n\nFor SVD mode, the input includes an exact factorization $J=U\\Sigma V^T$, or a computed report containing finite stored factors $\\widehat U_1$, $\\widehat\\Sigma=\\operatorname{diag}(\\widehat\\sigma_i)$ with nonnegative entries, and $\\widehat V$, together with certified intervals $[\\ell_i,u_i]$ satisfying $\\ell_i\\le\\sigma_i(J)\\le u_i$ for each of the $n$ singular values relevant to full column rank. In the exact case, if any $\\sigma_i\\le\\tau$, return rank-below-threshold and no Gauss-Newton step. If every $\\sigma_i>\\tau$, return\n$$p=-V\\,\\operatorname{diag}(\\sigma_1^{-1},\\ldots,\\sigma_n^{-1})\\,U_1^Tr,$$\nwhere $U_1$ consists of the corresponding $n$ left singular vectors. For a computed report, if any $u_i\\le\\tau$, return rank-below-threshold; if any interval satisfies $\\ell_i\\le\\tau<u_i$, return rank-unverified; if every lower endpoint exceeds $\\tau$ but some stored $\\widehat\\sigma_i=0$, return factorization-failure; otherwise return the finite candidate\n$$\\widehat p=-\\widehat V\\,\\operatorname{diag}(\\widehat\\sigma_1^{-1},\\ldots,\\widehat\\sigma_n^{-1})\\,\\widehat U_1^Tr$$\nwith status computed-candidate and make no accuracy claim beyond the supplied report. The certified intervals determine only the threshold branch; no computed-SVD accuracy bound is asserted. A computed SVD routine is not defined here; the SVD branch consumes its report.\n\nIf $m<n$, return unsupported-shape; if the selected factorization reports failure, return factorization-failure; every status other than exact-step is explicitly not a certified exact full-rank Gauss-Newton step.",
+          "quote": "Input a stored residual $r\\in\\mathbb R^m$, a stored Jacobian $J\\in\\mathbb R^{m\\times n}$ with $m,n\\ge1$ (using the convention of [[def-jacobian-matrix-and-gradient]]), a factorization mode QR or SVD, an arithmetic mode (exact or computed), and a declared singular-value threshold $\\tau\\ge0$. A computed QR report may also carry a verified full-rank certificate $s>0$ asserting $\\|Jv\\|_2\\ge s\\|v\\|_2$ for every $v\\in\\mathbb R^n$. The target exact step, when it is returned, is the unique minimizer of $\\frac12\\|r+Jp\\|_2^2$ and hence solves $J^TJp=-J^Tr$; this target is asserted only on a full-column-rank branch. Do not form $J^TJ$ in either solve path.\n\nFor QR mode the exact and computed routes are disjoint. Exact mode requires a supplied exact reduced factorization $J=QR$ with $Q^TQ=I_n$; only this exact factorization may reach the exact-step branch. Computed mode consumes a computed QR report or forms one by setting $C=[J\\mid-r]$ and, for $k=1,\\ldots,n$, applying [[alg-scaled-householder-reflector-formation-and-application]] to the active part of column $k$ and all trailing columns of $C$, including its last right-hand-side column. Propagate the first factorization failure. After a successful computed loop, the report consists of the computed upper-triangular block $\\widehat R$ and the first $n$ entries $\\widehat y$ of the transformed last column. These rounded outputs are not an exact factorization of $J$ and cannot be supplied to the exact branch. In exact mode, a zero diagonal in $R$ returns rank-deficient; otherwise solve $Rp=Q^T(-r)$ by backward substitution and return exact-step($p$). In computed mode, a zero diagonal returns rank-deficient-candidate. Otherwise initialize storage for $\\widehat p_0,\\ldots,\\widehat p_{n-1}$ with all components unassigned, then for $i=n-1,n-2,\\ldots,0$ compute $s_i$ by setting $s_i=0$ and, for $j=i+1,i+2,\\ldots,n-1$ in increasing order, updating $s_i\\leftarrow\\operatorname{fl}(s_i+\\operatorname{fl}(\\widehat R_{ij}\\widehat p_j))$; then compute $t_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\widehat y_i-s_i)$ and $\\widehat p_i=\\operatorname{fl}(t_i/\\widehat R_{ii})$. Any first arithmetic or range failure returns linear-solve-failure with its stage and indices. A nonzero computed diagonal without an independently verified full-rank certificate $s>0$ for the input matrix $J$ returns rank-unverified with the computed candidate but no full-rank claim. With that certificate, return computed-candidate($\\widehat p$). A nonzero computed diagonal alone is not a full-rank certificate. The computed-QR backward-stability conclusion of [[thm-computed-full-rank-least-squares-backward-stability]] is attached only when all of that theorem's successful-execution, arithmetic, and nonsingularity hypotheses are supplied; otherwise no backward-stability conclusion is returned.\n\nFor SVD mode, the input includes an exact factorization $J=U\\Sigma V^T$, or a computed report containing finite stored factors $\\widehat U_1$, $\\widehat\\Sigma=\\operatorname{diag}(\\widehat\\sigma_i)$ with nonnegative entries, and $\\widehat V$, together with certified intervals $[\\ell_i,u_i]$ satisfying $\\ell_i\\le\\sigma_i(J)\\le u_i$ for each of the $n$ singular values relevant to full column rank. In the exact case, if any $\\sigma_i\\le\\tau$, return rank-below-threshold and no Gauss-Newton step. If every $\\sigma_i>\\tau$, return\n$$p=-V\\,\\operatorname{diag}(\\sigma_1^{-1},\\ldots,\\sigma_n^{-1})\\,U_1^Tr,$$\nwhere $U_1$ consists of the corresponding $n$ left singular vectors. For a computed report, if any $u_i\\le\\tau$, return rank-below-threshold; if any interval satisfies $\\ell_i\\le\\tau<u_i$, return rank-unverified; if every lower endpoint exceeds $\\tau$ but some stored $\\widehat\\sigma_i=0$, return factorization-failure; otherwise return the finite candidate\n$$\\widehat p=-\\widehat V\\,\\operatorname{diag}(\\widehat\\sigma_1^{-1},\\ldots,\\widehat\\sigma_n^{-1})\\,\\widehat U_1^Tr$$\nwith status computed-candidate and make no accuracy claim beyond the supplied report. The certified intervals determine only the threshold branch; no computed-SVD accuracy bound is asserted. A computed SVD routine is not defined here; the SVD branch consumes its report.\n\nIf $m<n$, return unsupported-shape; if the selected factorization reports failure, return factorization-failure; every status other than exact-step is explicitly not a certified exact full-rank Gauss-Newton step.",
